##* {{RQ:John Heywood Proverbs|chapter=V|page=20|passage=''Of two ils chose the '''least''''', while choise lyeth in lot.}}
##* {{RQ:Sterne Sentimental Journey|volume=II|chapter=The Act of Charity. Paris.|pages=148–149|pageref=149|passage=At the end of it {{quote-gloss|a passage}}, tovvards the theatre, 'tis lighted by a ſmall candle, the light of vvhich is almoſt loſt before you get half-vvay dovvn, but near the door—'tis more for ornament than uſe: you ſee it as a fix'd ſtar of the '''leaſt''' magnitude; it burns—but does little good to the vvorld, that vve knovv of.}}
##* {{RQ:Ruskin Eagle's Nest|para=2|page=3|passage=[T]he '''least''' part of the work of any sound art-teacher must be his talking.}}
### Of [[two#Numeral|two]] or more [[animal#Noun|animals]] or [[plant#Noun|plants]] with the same [[name#Noun|name]]: the [[smaller#Adjective|smaller]] or smallest.
###: {{ux|en|[[least weasel|'''least''' weasel]]}}
###* {{RQ:Gerard Herball|chapter=Of Whiteblowe, or Whitlowe Grasse|page=498|passage=The firſt is a very ſlender plant hauing a fevve ſmall leaues like the '''leaſt''' Chickvveede, grovving in little tufts, from the midſt vvhereof riſeth vp a ſmall ſtalke, nine inches long; {{...}}}}
###* {{RQ:Gerard Herball|year=1633|chapter=Of Hedge Hyssope|pages=581–582|pageref=582|passage=[T]he floures of a purple colour, ſpotted on the inſide vvith vvhite, and of a brighter purple than the reſt of the floure, faſhioned like the ſmallest ''Anirrhinum'', or '''leaſt''' Snapdragon, {{...}}}}
## {{lb|en|archaic}} [[low#Adjective|Lowest]] in [[importance]] or [[status]]; [[most#Adverb|most]] [[insignificant#Adjective|insignificant]] or [[unimportant]].
##* {{RQ:De Mornay Sidney Golding Trewnesse|chapter=Preface|page=26|passage=[M]ans reaſon is ſo farre off from being the meaſurer of faith, vvhich very far exceedeth nature, that it is not ſo much as the meaſurer of nature, & of the '''leaſt''' creatures vvhich lie farre vnderneath man; becauſe of the ignorance and vntovvardnes vvhich is in vs and raigneth in vs.}}
##* {{RQ:Shakespeare Richard 3 Q1|act=V|scene=v|sig=M2|page=99|passage=But if I thriue, the gaine of my attempt, / The '''leaſt''' of you, ſhall ſhare his part thereof.}}
##* {{RQ:King James Version|Matthew|2|6|sig=A2|verso=1|page=1221|column=1|passage=And thou Bethlehem ''in'' the land of Juda, art not the '''leaſt''' among the Princes of Juda: for out of thee ſhall come a Gouernour, that ſhall rule my people Iſrael.}}
##* {{RQ:Jonson Catiline His Conspiracy|sig=M2|page=98|passage=Chiefly, vvhen this ſure ioy ſhall crovvne our ſide, / That the '''leaſt''' man, that falles vpon our party / This day {{...}} / Shall vvalke at pleaſure, in the tents of reſt; {{...}}}}
##* {{RQ:Robert Browning Dramatis Personae|stanza=2|page=248|passage=Take the '''least''' man of all mankind, as I; / Look at his head and heart, find how and why / He differs from his fellows utterly: {{...}}}}
